- HIGH — Service 200/hour limiting is raceable as specified. The packet says prune/count/insert, but does not require the `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` style atomic reservation the live gateway uses. Concurrent post-schema calls could pass the count before inserting. Refs: `.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md` §7 lines 320-326; `src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/gateway.rs` lines 602-675. Action: require atomic reserve/commit/rollback semantics for the service ledger, including dry runs and rejected live attempts after schema validation.

- HIGH — Failed write attempts after handler entry are not guaranteed to be audited. The live gateway audits only successful handler responses; handler errors return without audit. That would omit forensic records for traversal rejects, entity misses, service rate limits, failed idempotency replays, or ingestion failures unless W4-C adds its own sanitized audit. Refs: packet §6/§8 lines 202-224 and 269-274; `src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/gateway.rs` lines 390-451; `src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/audit.rs` lines 78-104. Action: require sanitized audit rows for all post-schema placement attempts, success and failure, with stable error code only.

- HIGH — Public idempotency handles are not required to be keyed opaque. The packet allows `document_handle` to be the idempotency id or an opaque derivative while the idempotency key includes `content_sha256`; an unkeyed digest/concatenation would let clients or logs test candidate content/entity replays. Refs: packet §6/§7 lines 196 and 278-333; `src-tauri/src/services/workspace_ingestion/pipeline.rs` lines 874-885. Action: require random UUIDs or server-secret HMACs for `idempotency_id`/`document_handle`, and forbid exposing any unkeyed content/path digest.

- MED — Dry-run mutation cursor shape is underspecified for privacy. Successful writes must include `mutation_cursor`, but dry runs intentionally create no idempotency/file/run rows. Returning `document_handle`, `idempotency_id`, or content-derived placeholders for dry run would persist a replayable fingerprint in response/audit without a durable mutation. Refs: packet §6/§7/§11 lines 168-200, 320-325, 395; `src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/taxonomy.rs` lines 176-189. Action: define a dry-run-only cursor with no durable handle and no content-derived value.

- MED — Non-Unix symlink/path behavior is not fail-closed in the packet. Live `open_validated` explicitly fails closed on non-Unix; the packet says final create uses no-follow only “where platform supports it,” which is too permissive for write placement. Refs: packet §6 lines 259-267; `src-tauri/src/services/workspace_ingestion/registry.rs` lines 37-39 and 154-159. Action: require fail-closed behavior on platforms without equivalent no-reparse/no-follow and parent canonicalization protections.

- MED — `source_asof_hint` “audit-only” is not actually guaranteed by live audit redaction. Write audits drop top-level params, so a hint carried only in params will not be audited, while storing it elsewhere risks confusing caller hint with trusted `source_asof`. Refs: packet §5/§10/§11 lines 162, 371, 389; `src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/audit.rs` lines 21-22 and 78-104. Action: either remove `source_asof_hint` from schema or explicitly audit only redacted hint metadata such as presence/parse validity, never as source attribution.

- MED — Migration slot `v280` is not reserved in the live wave plans. The packet moved to v280, but v1.4.5 reserves v250-v269 and v1.4.6 reserves v260-v279; no live coordination doc reserves v280 for DOS-474. Refs: packet §1/§7/§9 lines 19, 284, 348-350; `.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md` lines 238-243 and 270; `.docs/plans/v1.4.6-waves.md` lines 327 and 1065. Action: reserve v280 explicitly before implementation.

Final verdict: HOLD